{
  "requirement": "`AgentConfig` and its backend-specific configuration types implement Serde\nserialization and deserialization. An application can embed them in its own\nconfiguration types; serializing and deserializing a supported configuration\npreserves its settings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** `AgentConfig` and its backend-specific types implement Serde serialization and deserialization. An application can embed them in its own configuration types. Serializing and then deserializing a supported configuration preserves its settings.\n\n**Coverage.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` is the main test. It covers all three backends (Bedrock, OpenAI, Ollama).\n  - For each backend it deserializes a JSON value into `AgentConfig`, then asserts that `to_value` equals the original value. That checks the serialized form is exactly the input.\n  - It also round-trips through a JSON string and asserts the copy equals the original config. That is a real serialize and deserialize round trip.\n  - The inputs include nested credentials (`BedrockCredentials` with a session token), `api_key`, `api_key_env`, `endpoint`, `aws_profile`, `region`, and `options`. The `options` values include integers, floats, booleans, nested maps and mixed arrays.\n  - The backend-specific types (`BedrockConfig`, `OpenAiConfig`, `OllamaConfig`, `BedrockCredentials`, `OptionValue`) are reached through `AgentConfig`, so their Serde behavior is asserted.\n- `fn[configuration_debug_hides_credentials]` checks that `SecretString` serializes and deserializes transparently, as the plain string. It also checks that an unknown field is rejected.\n\n**Implementation.** All the types derive `Serialize` and `Deserialize`. `AgentConfig` uses `#[serde(tag = \"backend\")]`. The structs are plain derives with `skip_serializing_if` and `default` on optional fields. There is no hand-written conditional logic that the tests leave unexercised.\n\n**Residual items, not gaps.**\n- No test embeds `AgentConfig` in an application struct. This follows from the derived trait implementations, and the requirement asks for no distinct behavior there.\n- No test serializes a backend struct on its own, outside `AgentConfig`. The derives are the same ones `AgentConfig` uses to round-trip.\n- Omitted optional fields, such as an absent `session_token` or an OpenAI config without `model`, are not round-tripped. This is a repeat of the same derive behavior, not a separate obligation.\n\nThe tests adequately check the subject.",
